{title: Morning Has Broken}
{key: C}
{time: 3/4}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C]Morning has [Am]bro[Dm]ken [G]like the first [F]mor[C]ning
[Am]Blackbird has [Em]spo[F]ken [Em]like the first [Dm]bird[G]
[C]Praise for the [F]sin[**]ging! [C]Praise for the [Am]mor[Dm]ning!
[G]Praise for them, [C]sprin[F]ging [G]fresh from the [C]Word[**]!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C]Sweet the rain's [Am]new [Dm]fall [G]sunlit from [F]Hea[C]ven
[Am]Like the first [Em]dew [F]fall [Em]on the first [Dm]gras[G]s
[C]Praise for the [F]sweet[**]ness [C]of the wet [Am]gar[Dm]den
[G]Sprung in com[C]plete[F]ness [G]where his feet [C]pass[**].
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C]Mine is the [Am]sun[Dm]light, [G]mine is the [F]mor[C]ning
[Am]Born of the [Em]one [F]light [Em]Eden saw [Dm]play[G]
[C]Praise with e[F]la[**]tion, [C]praise every [Am]mor[Dm]ning
[G]God's recre[C]a[F]tion [G]of the new [C]day[**]!
{end_of_verse}
